  "solution": {
    "text": "Hematite is a common iron oxide with a formula of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> so Fe in it has +3 oxidation state.<br />Magnetite is a rock mineral and one of the main iron ores, with the chemical formula <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> .so it is a mixed oxide with oxidation states of Fe as +3 and +2.",
